Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; 26 - Microsoft Edge does not start with Windows and does not keep running after you close it.
; Edge normally starts a few of its processes at sign-in ("startup boost") and keeps them alive in
; the background after the last window is closed ("background mode"), so that it opens faster.
; That uses some memory and CPU while you play. These are two policies that Microsoft documents for
; Edge: StartupBoostEnabled and BackgroundModeEnabled, both set to 0 (off).
; Edge itself then shows "Your browser is managed by your organization", and the two switches in
; edge://settings/system are locked. Edge still works as before, it only opens a little slower.
; Undo: menu 7, then 26 (the two values are removed).
[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Edge]
"StartupBoostEnabled"=dword:00000000
"BackgroundModeEnabled"=dword:00000000
